WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.859
Zerodha's Blobasaur

00:00:01.895 --> 00:00:02.779
distributed

00:00:02.862 --> 00:00:04.135
high-performance blob

00:00:03.947 --> 00:00:05.774
storage on SQLite

00:00:06.294 --> 00:00:07.838
Zerodha built Blobasaur

00:00:07.992 --> 00:00:09.442
an open-source sharded

00:00:09.254 --> 00:00:10.173
blob server in

00:00:09.985 --> 00:00:11.058
Rust that speaks

00:00:10.869 --> 00:00:12.131
the Redis protocol

00:00:11.943 --> 00:00:13.098
and stores data

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:13.970
in SQLite

00:00:14.183 --> 00:00:15.362
serving thousands of

00:00:15.174 --> 00:00:17.095
multi-KB-to-MB JSON

00:00:16.907 --> 00:00:18.133
blob reads and

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:19.194
writes per second

00:00:19.726 --> 00:00:20.315
Kite

00:00:20.434 --> 00:00:22.096
Zerodha's trading platform

00:00:21.908 --> 00:00:22.921
with about 20

00:00:22.733 --> 00:00:23.817
million customers

00:00:23.936 --> 00:00:25.339
stores chart layouts

00:00:25.457 --> 00:00:26.589
indicator templates

00:00:26.401 --> 00:00:28.134
and workspace preferences

00:00:27.945 --> 00:00:29.195
as opaque blobs

00:00:29.007 --> 00:00:29.773
from a few

00:00:29.584 --> 00:00:30.810
KB to several

00:00:30.622 --> 00:00:31.259
MB.

00:00:31.790 --> 00:00:35.292
At 25,324 HSET

00:00:35.104 --> 00:00:36.542
operations per second

00:00:36.814 --> 00:00:37.745
each carrying a

00:00:37.556 --> 00:00:39.290
64 KiB payload

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:40.870
Blobasaur processes

00:00:40.681 --> 00:00:43.700
roughly 1.66 GB/s of

00:00:43.606 --> 00:00:45.256
uncompressed JSON through

00:00:45.068 --> 00:00:46.035
zstd

00:00:46.566 --> 00:00:47.580
Full story on

00:00:47.391 --> 00:00:48.287
the dashboard
